{
  "about": "How an SDK names the error on a span the Anthropic SDK made itself (instrumentation scope com.anthropic.sdk. and anything after it, every platform client included). That SDK sets error.type to the code in the API's error envelope (not_found_error) or, without one, the HTTP status. The SDK's normalization replaces it with the exception class the Anthropic SDK raises for the span's http.response.status_code, spelled as the SDKs spell an exception class elsewhere (anthropic.NotFoundError), so the same failure groups under one name whether or not the OpenInference instrumentation is on. Only the statuses every Anthropic client in both languages raises the same class for are mapped: 400, 401, 403, 404, 409, 422 and 429 to their own classes, and every 5xx except 503, 504 and 529 to anthropic.InternalServerError. 413, 503, 504 and 529 raise different classes per client or language, so they keep error.type as it is, as does any other status. A span with no status also keeps it: a connection error, a timeout, and the SDK's own spans around API calls (the tool runner's invoke_agent span, environment work), which record the failed call's error code but not its status. The chat span inside them carries the status and is mapped. An error event on a stream that opened with 200, and a span from any other scope, keep it too. `scope` is the span's instrumentation scope name, `attributes` its attributes as it ends (an ERROR status), and `expected` the error.type it is exported with.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "bad_request",
      "scope": "com.anthropic.sdk.python",
      "attributes": {
        "error.type": "invalid_request_error",
        "http.response.status_code": 400
      },
      "expected": "anthropic.BadRequestError"
    },
    {
      "name": "authentication",
      "scope": "com.anthropic.sdk.python",
      "attributes": {
        "error.type": "authentication_error",
        "http.response.status_code": 401
      },
      "expected": "anthropic.AuthenticationError"
    },
    {
      "name": "permission_denied",
      "scope": "com.anthropic.sdk.python",
      "attributes": {
        "error.type": "permission_error",
        "http.response.status_code": 403
      },
      "expected": "anthropic.PermissionDeniedError"
    },
    {
      "name": "not_found",
      "scope": "com.anthropic.sdk.python",
      "attributes": {
        "error.type": "not_found_error",
        "http.response.status_code": 404
      },
      "expected": "anthropic.NotFoundError"
    },
    {
      "name": "conflict",
      "scope": "com.anthropic.sdk.python",
      "attributes": {
        "error.type": "conflict_error",
        "http.response.status_code": 409
